% Public domain beginner songs, typed from memory: so-mi-la chants, do-re-mi
% songs and the first diatonic classroom songs. Traditional unless a composer
% is named; every composer named died well over a century ago.
% Checked 11 November 2026: Bounce High, Rain Rain, Rocky Mountain and Go Tell
% Aunt Rhody against the Kodaly teaching transcriptions of the American folk
% versions (150 American Folk Songs and its addenda); This Old Man against the
% BBC's Singing Together (1970), with the American "with a" pickup.
% Skip to My Lou has its long "Lou, Lou" (two beats each). Words now
% fit their notes one syllable to a note, _ marking a syllable held over two.

